  "findings": [
    {
      "id": "LIFECYCLE-PROBE-PUBLICATION",
      "status": "STATIC_GUARDS_PRESENT",
      "details": "The wrapper lowers shutdown and marks probe incomplete before the stock-exact body. Probe completion is published only after workqueue, firmware work, buffers, LED/sysfs and node setup succeed. File open requires probe completion, so the misc device cannot expose partial state. Failures raise shutdown and route through cleanup."
    },
    {
      "id": "LIFECYCLE-EARLY-IRQ",
      "status": "STATIC_DEFAULT_PATH_REVIEWED_RUNTIME_UNVERIFIED",
      "details": "Stock probe assigns the function table and initializes the chip before irq_config, then registers the IRQ before timer/workqueue initialization and RTP/FIFO allocation. State allocation flags 0xdc0 include __GFP_ZERO in the pinned target headers. The candidate IRQ wrapper has shutdown and mutex gates but no probe_complete gate, so early IRQ remains possible. In the stock handler, zero rtp_loop at +0x6bc and RAM-ready byte at +5 gate the FIFO and RAM branches on the pre-publication default path. This is static ordering evidence only."
    },
    {
      "id": "LIFECYCLE-RAM-WORKER",
      "status": "PREPROBE_WORK_GATED_AND_RETRY_STATICALLY_CONFIRMED",
      "details": "The first RAM worker is queued after 2000 jiffies (8 seconds at HZ=250). Before probe completion, the candidate avoids RAM-state mutation and firmware submission, requeues after 250 jiffies (1 second) only while shutdown is false, then returns."
    },
    {
      "id": "LIFECYCLE-FIRMWARE-CALLBACK",
      "status": "TRACKED_DRAIN_STATICALLY_CONFIRMED",
      "details": "The request helper counts callbacks before request_firmware_nowait, passes THIS_MODULE, rechecks shutdown, and rolls back on shutdown or synchronous submission failure. Completion serializes ram_load, releases firmware on shutdown, then decrements/wakes the drain. Pinned loader calls completion before module_put; pinned release_firmware accepts NULL."
    },
    {
      "id": "LIFECYCLE-REMOVE",
      "status": "CALLBACK_TIMER_AND_WORK_DRAINS_STATICALLY_CONFIRMED",
      "details": "aw_remove blocks new file access, waits active operations, unregisters the LED child to drain sysfs, cancels RAM delayed work, drains firmware callbacks, and cancels delayed work again. The null-workqueue wait is the mutually exclusive branch where ram_work_init never ran. It drains published FIFO/TikTap work, frees IRQ as applicable, cancels both hrtimers and their work twice, destroys the queue, and retires state/pages."
    },
